the two aren't all  that different almost identical even so  what purpose does the surface have left  and besides providing solid footing when  you're not soaring in the skies above of  course it is from ground level that will  be gaining access to some of the islands  as seen in the example where link  rewinds a piece of Fallen Sky debris and  rides it up to the island it originated  from but this is just a means by which  to escape the surface so what about  Hyrule itself are there new things to  explore here new Dungeons and challenges  nine thousand korok seats this time no  God please no no  I think there may be a lot more to  Hyrule surface than the promotional  material has led on so far though it may  look very similar from a distance you  can't judge a book by its cover so let's  go over some of the possibilities do  keep in mind that just like with the  main story most of what I'm about to  talk about is highly speculative and may  not reflect the final product in fact it  probably won't with that said let's get  into it in the footage presented so far  tears of the Kingdom's surface has been  shown quite sparingly and when it does  show up it's in specific lighting and  from clever camera angles that make it  difficult to see the finer details  despite this we have been able to spot a  few changes over the past years ever  since the game's review in 2019 the most  notable of which are that the shika  towers and shrines are no longer present  Hyrule Castle has been ripped from its  foundation and is now suspended in the  air by ganon's malice the Deku Tree and  possibly the entire great Forest are no  longer where they should be there are  strange pieces of debris scattered about  which weren't there before and death  Mountain's lava flow has seemingly run  dry the mystery behind the last two of  these observations have now been cleared  up by the Third teaser the unknown  debris is confirmed to originate from  the floating islands and as mentioned  before you can use them to hitch a ride  up Death Mountain has dried up because  it's plugged up by malice which can be  seen boiling up from the summit but  there's another big change which a lot  of people initially missed for good  reason because it's not actually shown  in the teaser itself but instead in the  official artwork Nintendo made public  shortly after the teaser went live here  too we see the malice written Death  Mountain the floating Hyrule castle and  another peculiar site a gigantic Vortex  covering a large area west of the castle  judging from the size comparison to the  other two landmarks this storm has to be  about the same size if not bigger than  Death Mountain itself which on its own  is so massive that it almost takes up an  entire Province there's still a debate  going on in regards to which part of the  map specifically has been engulfed by  this giant storm there's been  suggestions of the hebra mountains Rito  Village the Forgotten Temple some even  think it may be as far south as Satori  Mountain I personally believe that  anything below Rito Village is  improbable if we line up the positions  in the artwork we can see that the storm  is approximately to the West maybe  slightly Northwest of the castle this  would place it somewhere in this general  area we can also see a long canyon-like  depression in the landscape between the  vortex and the castle and if I had to  guess this would have to be tanagar  Canyon the giant Gorge that spans from  the Gerudo Highlands in the South all  the way up North and separates Central  Hyrule from The hebra Province if this  is indeed tanagar Canyon this eliminates  places like Satori and the Forgotten  Temple and narrows it down to hebra  alone as it's the only province that  lies west of the canyon my top two  contenders right now are Rito Village  and the hebra peak and I'm currently  leaning more towards the ladder for a  couple of reasons primarily the fact  that we don't see hebra Peak anywhere in  