f the changes we've been able  to spot so far all correlate to specific  people or factions from breath of the  wild the Hylian seed of power Death  Mountain Home of the gorons the missing  Deku Tree Spirit guardian of the koroks  and now this giant storm potentially  terrorizing the Rito I don't think I'm  alone when I say that there seems to be  a pattern here these are all beings and  factions who stood against Ganon in some  way either providing support on the day  of the Calamity or 100 years after the  apocalypse when the hero woke up for a  rematch now that the true face behind  the Calamity Ganondorf himself is back  in the flesh it is to be expected that  he would Target those who foiled his  scheme to take over Hyrule these four  factions already checked the box but  there's also the Gerudo shika and the  Zora the total number of races that  stood against Ganon and currently still  inhabit Hyrule amounts to seven I'm  excluding the yiga as they are basically  just chica turned evil is it a  coincidence then that we happen to see  this god-like figure surrounded by seven  orbs many have made the connection that  the seven orbs could correspond to 7 and  dungeons with a possible eighth and  final one as Zelda games tend to have  the numbers 7 and 8 are quite prevalent  in breath of the Wild and the series as  a whole for that matter the most notable  are the seven heroine statues plus the  secret eighth heroine which is said to  have been wiped from history we have all  the imagery referencing the seven sages  the seven races of the Kingdom with the  zonai possibly being the missing eighth  not to mention breath the Wild's Hyrule  is divided into eight provinces the only  problem is we haven't seen substantial  footage of any location belonging to the  other factions there's not a single  frame of Zora's domain kakariko Village  which is barely visible in this shot is  too far away to confirm any changes and  the home of the Gerudo is obscured by  the highlands that wrap around the  entire Province so we can't say for sure  if these areas are also struck by  disaster the pattern suggests that they  probably are but right now we have no  proof of this of course the fact that we  don't see these afflictions from afar in  some of these wide charts doesn't mean  they don't exist for all we know the  Waters of zoro's domain could be  poisoned or something and the guru are  being tortured by an endless loop of the  rude Sandstorm the orbs depicted on the  mural could represent some sort of  balance or stability a balance which  could have been corrupted by Ganondorf  leading to all kinds of disasters across  hyrule's provinces and in order to cure  this imbalance link has to visit some  sort of ancient temples or shrines to  well you know how it generally goes into  other games another possibility is that  these orbs are the key to restoring the  master sword in some way which Ganondorf  is aware of and the many calamities  plaguing these regions are simply him  trying to prevent link from getting to  them if there are indeed bigger more  classic dungeons present in tears of the  Kingdom I think it's more than possible  that most if not all of them are found  on the surface or below it as opposed to  in the skies above it would give a new  and important purpose to the lands of  Hyrule it's one more reason why I chose  hebra Peak as my Prime candidate for the  eye of the storm as opposed to Rito  Village as it would be a perfect  location to house a secret Temple of  sorts we have proof that the hebra  mountains have all sorts of caves and  secret Chambers inside them some of them  hidden behind man-made doors like the  enormous cave that houses one of the  great skeletons so what about the  islands in the sky then what purpose  would they serve if dungeons end up  being on the surface below well it could  be that the means to access these  ancient temples are obtained here like  certain powers for Link's new bracelet  for example it's not uncommon for a  Zelda game to hide key items necessary  to gain access to a dungeon somewhere  else in the Overworld by traveling to  the sky and learning new abilities you  would be able to unlock new areas at  ground level now this may sound like it  would be an extremely linear experience  but that doesn't have to be the case at  all if you can visit the many islands in  any order you please it means that the  dungeons too can be tackled in any order  just like in breath of the wild it goes  without saying that this is all  conjecture maybe dungeons are present in  the sky maybe the surface World serves a  completely different purpose maybe these  are just stylistic depictions of a  loincloth you may have noticed while  talking about this stuff happening on  the surface that I primarily used  footage from the newest teaser as  opposed to the other two this is because  in the older footage some things we've  talked about like the storm in hebra are  different or not yet present we can see  hebra Peak right behind the castle in  this shot and yet there's nothing  unusual about it while it could be that  this takes place earlier in the story  before some of these cataclysms manifest  it's also obvious that Nintendo is  constantly adding things and making  changes to the game as they go along  Death Mountain initially didn't have  malice erupting from its Summit the  bottom of the floating islands used to  look like natural rock formations while  in the recent footage most of them have  these man-made antennas all of a sudden  and there are many more examples of  changes and things being moved around as  development progresses which is only  natural I mean think back at how  different breath of the wild looked in  some of the early footage all we can do  is guess which is a big part of the fun  of anticipation at least for me and  there's so much more to theorize about  by the looks of it tears of the Kingdom  as one of the broadest set of goals and  Mysteries in any Zelda game to date the  broken Master Sword the curse on Link's  arm Zelda's disappearance and if and how  we'll get her back the catastrophe is  inflicted on Hiro's people the mystery  and Legacy of the zonai so on and so  forth anyway that is all for today a big  shout out to my mods Discord Community  everyone who's been sharing ideas and  theories with me in the past week or so  and of course my patreons and channel  members of which William Charles and Sam  T joined recently so a big thanks to the  both of you it means a lot I have plenty  of ideas to work with in the coming  weeks so I hope you look forward to  future videos this is Don signing off  and have a good one  [Music]  foreign thank you  [Music]

